{3}$ involves multiplying a row by $3,$ so the determinant is multiplied by $3$ as well.\n\nTherefore, we have to change the sign of the determinant to the opposite one and multiply by $3$ as well. Consequently, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =3\\cdot (-det(A)) \\\\  & =-3det(A) \\\\  & =-3\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =-15.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534936 true] [17592186320979 1000 #edb/ref 17592186320980 13194139534936 true] [17592186320979 1000 #edb/ref 17592186320981 13194139534936 true] [17592186320979 1000 #edb/ref 17592186320982 13194139534936 true] [17592186320979 1000 #edb/ref 17592186320983 13194139534936 true] [17592186320979 1000 #edb/ref 17592186320984 13194139534936 true] [17592186320979 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534936 true] [17592186320979 1041 "selection" 13194139534936 true] [17592186320979 1104 #edb/ref 17592186320980 13194139534936 true] [17592186320979 1110 #uuid "7fa0b0c4-4f81-5062-ae85-deed1cca5e2a" 13194139534936 true] [17592186320980 1034 "-15" 13194139534936 true] [17592186320980 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534936 true] [17592186320980 1111 #uuid "b1548f75-0eff-5eea-8b46-e55cde11d63a" 13194139534936 true] [17592186320981 1034 "-5" 13194139534936 true] [17592186320981 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534936 true] [17592186320981 1111 #uuid "9d367593-e2ab-5817-b8cc-6fea2afa470a" 13194139534936 true] [17592186320982 1034 "-20" 13194139534936 true] [17592186320982 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534936 true] [17592186320982 1111 #uuid "43db3489-ff1f-5ea0-a124-e7723ae72ba9" 13194139534936 true] [17592186320983 1034 "15" 13194139534936 true] [17592186320983 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534936 true] [17592186320983 1111 #uuid "4f42c278-df08-5d68-8999-6b3648da8d0c" 13194139534936 true] [17592186320984 1034 "5" 13194139534936 true] [17592186320984 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534936 true] [17592186320984 1111 #uuid "8ee4e258-49d1-5a49-9cc6-1bddc927f387" 13194139534936 true] [17592186320985 1017 #edb/ref 1759